      "legal.datenschutzTitle": "Privacy Policy",
      "legal.datenschutz": "<strong>1. Data Controller</strong><br>Sagacitas Ltd, 136 Capel Street, Dublin, Ireland (company registration number: to be added once incorporation is complete). Contact: <a href=\"mailto:info@degaja.com\">info@degaja.com</a><br><br><strong>2. What data we process</strong><br>Information provided when creating an account (name, email) is stored only locally in your browser and is never transmitted to or stored by us; your questions and the answers DEGAJA generates, in order to provide the service; payment data (processed exclusively by our payment provider — we do not store card details); technical information such as your language preference, also stored locally in your browser.<br><br><strong>3. Legal bases</strong><br>Performance of a contract (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)), legitimate interest (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f), e.g. fraud prevention), and consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)) for optional features such as voice playback.<br><br><strong>4. Third-party providers (data processors)</strong><br>We work with carefully selected external providers for payment processing, AI-based answer generation, optional voice synthesis, internal notifications, and hosting. Some of these providers are located outside the EU (mainly the US); transfers are based on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.<br><br><strong>5. Retention period</strong><br>We keep data only as long as necessary for the purposes described, or as required by law.<br><br><strong>6. Your rights</strong><br>You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing of, port, and object to the processing of your data. Contact <a href=\"mailto:info@degaja.com\">info@degaja.com</a> for any of these requests. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection authority (in Ireland: the Data Protection Commission).<br><br><strong>7. Cookies / local storage</strong><br>We use localStorage in your browser, e.g. to remember your language preference. We do not use tracking cookies for advertising purposes.<br><br><strong>8. Age restriction</strong><br>DEGAJA is intended exclusively for users aged 18 and over.<br><br><strong>9. Changes</strong><br>We may update this privacy policy as needed. The current version is always available on this page.",
      "legal.agbTitle": "Terms & Conditions",
      "legal.agb": "<strong>1. Scope</strong><br>These Terms apply to the use of the DEGAJA website and services, operated by Sagacitas Ltd, Dublin, Ireland.<br><br><strong>2. Nature of the service</strong><br>DEGAJA offers personal guidance through tarot, astrology and numerology for entertainment purposes. Our content does not replace professional medical, legal, financial or psychological advice, and does not constitute a guaranteed prediction of future events.<br><br><strong>3. Age restriction</strong><br>Use of this service is restricted to persons aged 18 and over.<br><br><strong>4. Formation of contract and services</strong><br>Purchasing a reading or package forms a contract for the provision of that specific digital service. The scope is as described on the website at the time of purchase.<br><br><strong>5. Prices and payment</strong><br>All prices include applicable taxes unless stated otherwise. Payment is processed through our payment provider.<br><br><strong>6. Right of withdrawal for digital content</strong><br>As this is digital content delivered immediately upon purchase, your statutory right of withdrawal ends once you expressly consent to immediate performance and acknowledge that you thereby lose your right of withdrawal (in accordance with EU Directive 2011/83/EU on consumer rights).<br><br><strong>7. Limitation of liability</strong><br>We are not liable for decisions made based on content received through DEGAJA. Use of the service is at your own responsibility.<br><br><strong>8. Changes to these Terms</strong><br>We may update these Terms as needed. The version published at the time of use applies.<br><br><strong>9. Governing law and jurisdiction</strong><br>Irish law applies. The courts of Dublin, Ireland have jurisdiction, to the extent permitted by law.<br><br><strong>10. Contact</strong><br>For questions about these Terms: <a href=\"mailto:info@degaja.com\">info@degaja.com</a>",
